s are transduced into cells through the integrin bound protein-tyrosine kinases. PTK2 (protein-tyrosine kinase 2, also known as Focal adhesion kinase 1; FADK1, FAK) is one of the protein tyrosine kinases that plays a prominent role in integrin signaling. PTK2 has been implicated in controlling cell motility and transmitting a cell survival signal from ECM. <br><br>PTK2 is recruited to sites of integrin clustering by directly binding to integrin associated c-Src.<br>", "literatureReference": [354120, 354182, 377572], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "updateTrackers": [{"dbId": 9778377, "displayName": "Update Tracker - [Reaction:354066] Translocation of PTK2 to Focal complexes - v68:[modifyText]", "action": ["modifyText"], "updatedInstance": [354066], "className": "UpdateTracker", "schemaClass": "UpdateTracker"}, {"dbId": 9790262, "displayName": "Update Tracker - [Reaction:354066] Translocation of PTK2 to Focal complexes - v34:[modifyText]", "action": ["modifyText"], "updatedInstance": [354066], "className": "UpdateTracker", "schemaClass": "UpdateTracker"}], "category": "binding", "input": [{"dbId": 201621, "displayName": "PTK2 [cytosol]", "stId": "R-HSA-201621", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-201621.2", "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["PTK2", "FAK1", "FADK1", "FAK", "Focal adhesion kinase 1"], "speciesName": "Homo sapiens", "catalystActivities": [{"dbId": 376142, "displayName": "protein tyrosine kinase activity of PTK2 [cytosol]", "physicalEntity": 201621, "className": "CatalystActivity", "schemaClass": "CatalystActivity"}], "consumedByEvent": [354066], "species": 48887, "endCoordinate": 1052, "referenceType": "ReferenceGeneProduct", "startCoordinate": 2, "className": "Protein", "inDisease": false, "schemaClass": "EntityWithAccessionedSequence"}, {"dbId": 377622, "displayName": "